    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d724">

                <pb facs="0879" n="791" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg791"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">338.1121 Zrike Bros. and Johnson/36:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-25T15:00:00-05:00">April 25, 1933—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>49. Reference Department’s telegram No. 30, April 24, 5 p.m., De la Rue informs
                    me that he has never given the impression to accused’s <pb facs="0880" n="792"
                        xml:id="pg792"/> attorney that he would participate in any settlement
                    negotiation and specifically referred the attorney to the Haitian Government for
                    any such discussion. He takes the position, in which I concur, that it would be
                    most improper for him to play any part in negotiations looking to a compromise
                    settlement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
